6. Registered or required to be registered
Paragraph 9-5(d) of the GST Act provides that to make a taxable supply you must be registered or required to be registered for GST.
Logically enough, ‘you are registered’ means registered for GST in accordance with the GST Act.
Section 23-5 of the GST Act provides that you must register for GST if:
•	you are carrying on an enterprise
•	your GST turnover meets the registration turnover threshold.
The registration turnover threshold for non-profit bodies is $150,000. The registration turnover threshold for other entities is $75,000.
There are special rules that require some entities to register for GST regardless of their turnover.
