These are some of the facts from Crees v Federal Commissioner of Taxation (2001) 46 ATR 1091; 2001 ATC 2021 (Crees Case).

After hearing evidence, the tribunal stated that the taxpayer may at some future time make a profit of $5,000 per annum. It concluded that the net effect of this was nil return from labour by two people for over 25 years.

