8. Special rules
The special rules may:
•	make an acquisition creditable even if it does not meet the requirements under the basic rules
•	make an acquisition non-creditable even if it does meet the requirements under the basic rules
•	make an entity other than the recipient entitled to the input tax credit
•	change the way the input tax credit is calculated.
Part 4-2 of the GST Act contains most of the special rules for creditable acquisitions. There are also special rules relating to creditable acquisitions in other provisions of the GST Act.
Section 11-99 lists all the special rules about creditable acquisitions.
