10. Time limit for claiming input tax credits
10.1 Division 93 of the GST Act
Division 93 of the GST Act contains special rules limiting the time you have to claim an input tax credit.
The time period imposed by Division 93 may impact the ability to amend an assessment under Subdivision 155-B of Schedule 1 to the TAA.
Generally, an entity's entitlement to an input tax credit ceases if it is not taken into account in their assessment within 4 years of the date they were required to lodge their GST return for the tax period to which it would be attributable under sections 29-10(1) and (2) of the GST Act.
There are some exceptions.
