You advise Chris that a letter will be sent confirming what has been discussed.
Scenario 5 - question
Is there anything else you should tell Chris?
Scenario 5 - debrief
To provide the best possible taxpayer experience it is appropriate to confirm that Chris, the trustee, is aware of the possibility of a debt as a result of the imposition of the penalty. You should prompt them to consider appropriate actions to take control of managing their affairs to address the debt.
Informing Chris on where to find information on ‘How to pay’ will assist them in their planning to manage their obligations.
To provide the best possible taxpayer experience you can confirm that Chris is aware of the individual/s responsible for addressing the potential liability.
Ensuring that Chris is aware that the penalty cannot be paid or reimbursed from the assets of the fund but rather must be paid by directors of a corporate trustees / individual trustees, enables them to plan.
