A new approach
INGOT (Information Notices and Garnishee Online Tool) has been specifically designed to facilitate an electronic exchange of information with financial institutions. It is used to issue information gathering and garnishee notices to enabled financial institutions.
Responses to these notices will also be received electronically and be accessible from within INGOT.
How the process works
•	An INGOT Request Officer will complete appropriate fields in INGOT with:
-	the details for the notice e.g., legislative provision
-	the details for the financial institution to use to match a client in their databases, and
-	the details of what we require them to provide, in the case of an information gathering notice, or action that needs to be taken in accordance with a garnishee notice. 
•	All INGOT requests are managed electronically by the financial institution. Some may require manual intervention (depending on the nature of the request). Once complete, a response is prepared and returned to the ATO.
•	At agreed periods throughout the day, submitted requests in INGOT will be batched and sent to the receiving financial institution.
•	Responses prepared by the financial institution are batched and returned to us on an agreed batching schedule and will appear in INGOT for review and further action as required. You will receive an email notifying you when a response has been received.

Launching INGOT
Access to INGOT will be provided upon completion of the relevant INGOT training packages.
Once access has been provided you will be able to launch INGOT via the appropriate hyperlink http://ingot/.
We recommend that you save this hyperlink as a favourite so that when access is provided you can access it easily and as required.
