Audit reviews
The Audit review is used to review our original audit decision in a recently closed streamlined audit case. The 
taxpayer has 30 days to request a review and provide us with documents to substantiate their claims. Audit 
reviews are conducted by case officers in BAS I&I.
An Audit review is generally restricted to recently closed high volume pre-issue audit, high-volume audit 
streamlined and high volume non-lodgement streamlined cases, where a liability was raised and the decision to 
raise the liability was made:
• without being able to contact the taxpayer, or
• when the taxpayer did not provide the documents and/or information as requested.
The outcome of an audit review will be one of the following three possibilities:
• reversal of our original decision in full
• partial reversal of our original decision, or
• original decision upheld.
•Requests for an audit review – Streamlined Audit Treatment - Inbound Calls
•Discuss with your team leader who will refer to the SB A&A Informal Review mailbox.
