INTERNAL
Why we request information
Businesses issue tax invoices to all customers where a sale is made and:
• Tax invoices must be issued upon request where the taxable sale exceeds $82.50 (inc GST)
• A client must hold a tax invoice at the time of making a claim for the GST credit (ie. when they lodge their BAS).
Requirements of a document to be a valid tax invoice:
• Document is intended to be a tax invoice
• The date the tax invoice was issued
• The seller’s identity and their ABN must be present
• GST amount (if any) payable, either shown separately or a statement that the total price includes GST 
• Quantity, price and brief description of the items sold
• The extent to which each item on the tax invoice is a taxable sale
• The buyer’s identity or ABN (if the sale is over $1,000)
Tax invoices for mixed supplies must clearly show which items are taxable.
Invoices for mixed supplies must clearly show which items are taxable.
