GST transaction listing
A GST transaction listing contains an itemised list of all the client’s transactions which should equal the amounts they have reported on their 
BAS. We request this to determine if the client is entitled to all the GST credits they’ve reported on their BAS. ie. the listing will show us if 
they are claiming purchases which are personal in nature like alcohol.
The GST transaction listing should include the following:
• The date the transaction occurred 
• A description of the transaction 
• The dollar amount of the transaction 
• The amount of GST included in the transaction
• Totals underneath each list of transactions 
