Bank statements can be used to verify that sales have been reported, and the payment of purchases.
Particularly important when dealing with clients that report on a cash basis, and where transactions involve related entities.
When you receive bank statements, confirm:
• The statement is in the name of the client
• Does the amount reported at label G1 match or exceed the amount deposited into the account
• Do debits from the account correlate to purchases reported
• Cross reference the bank statement and the GST transaction list because you should be able to see most, if not all, of the transactions 
in the GST transaction list in the bank statement.
