‘Improving information and evidence gathering’
“I have a strong view that the tax officer should maintain a very strict file noting system. That is, every 
discussion with the taxpayer should be recorded by the Tax Officer, written down, signed and dated 
and put on the file. 
Why? Well first of all officers, go, depart, change and it needs to be recorded.
Secondly, we are living in a world which I think in the last five or ten years of my exposure to the tax 
field, taxpayers have become much more attune at challenging the conduct of the Tax Office. If there 
is a file note recording what transpired, then the dispute is at least minimised. It will not be completely 
removed. I accept that, but at least it will be minimised. That includes discussions over the 
telephone."
Justice Michelle Gordon, March 2007
