'TP T/A RE TP. T/A UNA. LMTBC'
1.'TP' has been used twice to mean different things – taxpayer and telephone.
2.'T/A' has at least two different meanings – tax agent and trading as.
3.'RE' could be short for regarding or an abbreviation of a name.
4.'UNA' is not a commonly known abbreviation.
5.'LMTBC' is also not a consistently used initialism. Some areas use LMTRB or LMTCB
'Telephoned tax agent regarding taxpayer. Tax agent unavailable. Left message to be called/contacted.
The original message, whilst concise, is not clear, correct or complete.
