Structuring your writing
If you organise what you write and structure it well, you will make it easier for the reader to read and understand 
what you have written.
The best way to organise your information will depend on the type of note you are recording. A useful tool to 
keep in mind is the five Ws.
• Who (did you speak to?)
• When (did you speak to them?)
• What (was discussed?)
• Why (did you make a decision?)
• Where (to from here?)
