Contact the client inline with the Client Contact Guide and Managing third party fraud in Small Business cases
Ensure you have made reasonable attempts to contact. 
- First attempt to be made within two business days of case allocation. 
- At least two further attempts on separate days and at different times.
• Using Extensive PORO to ensure that you’re speaking with the client and not with a third party purporting to be the client
• Go into the conversation without prejudice and firstly confirm if they are aware of the BAS lodgments and confirm if the contact details we have 
for the client are correct
• Do not provide details of information held by the ATO to seek confirmation. In effect, this will demonstrate if the client is aware of any changes to 
their digital record, GST and ABN registration, activity statement and income tax lodgements or amendments, or a recent appointment as Director 
of a Company or Trustee of a Trust.
• Once you have completed your investigation, a finalisation letter needs to be sent to the taxpayer before further referrals are done.
