What are we looking for when profiling?
We are looking for information that helps us to get an understanding of the client and to assist us identifying risks that need to 
be tested. Using information available to us from internal and external systems.
As a general guide, we look at:
• Signs of enterprise 
• Recent interactions with the ATO
• Previous compliance history 
• Periods under review and BAS lodgment patterns 
• Checks for signs of third-party fraud
The type of case you are working on determines the level of profiling and what to look for. 
It is important not to over profile as we don’t want to over analyse a client, make assumptions or gather information that is not 
relevant. In most work types, you will be contacting the taxpayer, to gain a better understanding from them about their business
and what they have reported on their activity statement.
