What is risk?
• Simply put, risk is the chance of danger or loss.
• When crossing a busy road, the risk is the chance that you will get hit by a car. If you have to cross the road, you cannot 
eliminate the risk. But you can manage it. For example, by crossing at the traffic lights.
From a SB A&A perspective, it is the chance that:
– A refund claimed is incorrect (risk to revenue) 
– An unauthorised third party lodged the AS 
• Our cases are created because they are flagged by the risk model
• Additional risks may be identified during profiling of a case or as the case progresses
• To complete a case, we need to address the risks associated with the case.
