About taxable sales
If you are registered for GST, or required to be, the goods and services you sell in Australia are taxable, unless they are GST-free or 
input-taxed.
To be a taxable sale with GST in the price, a sale must be:
• for payment of some kind
• made in the course of operating your business
• connected with Australia.
For a sale to be taxable, you must provide the goods or services as part of conducting your business. This includes all sales of
business assets, including items such as motor vehicles and office plant and equipment. It also includes things done in the course 
of setting up or winding down your business.
