UNOFFICIAL
UNOFFICIAL
Answer: Question 
It means that a supply can be partly taxable and partly GST-free or input taxed.
For example, if you sell a:
• Pair of glasses, the lenses are GST-free while the frames are taxable
• Property that consists of a shop on the ground floor with a flat above, the flat is input taxed while the shop is taxable.
