INTERNAL
GST-free sales
Most basic foods, some education courses and some medical, health and care products and services are GST-free, often referred 
to as exempt from GST. 
Things that are GST-free include:
• Most basic food
• Education courses, course materials and related excursions or field trips
• Medical, health and care services
• Childcare services
• Sales of businesses as going concern
• Exports
• Activities of charities
• Farmland
• Water, sewerage and drainage
• Cars for disabled people to use, when certain requirements are met
UNOFFICIAL
UNOFFICIAL
Input tax supplies
Input-taxed sales don’t include GST in the price and cannot claim GST credits. 
The most common input-taxed sales are financial supplies (such as lending money or the provision of credit for a fee) and 
selling or renting out residential premises.
Financial supplies – Financial supplies made by a registered entity will be input taxed. General rule for entities making inputtaxed supplies is that there is no entitlement to input tax credits are input-taxed sales.
Residential premises – Selling or renting existing residential premises are input-taxed sales and do not include GST. However, if 
the residential premise is considered 'new', it is a taxable sale and GST is applicable. If you buy property - old or new - with the 
intention of selling it at a profit or developing it to sell, you may be considered to be carrying on a business and may be required 
to register for GST.
Generally, you are not considered to be carrying on a business if your property transactions are for private purposes such as
when you are constructing or selling your family home
