Tax Periods
Under the general rule in section 27-5, the standard tax period reporting is 
quarterly. All taxpayer’s may elect to have a one month tax period apply.
Monthly – Must report monthly if your GST turnover is $20 million or more.
Quarterly – if your GST turnover is less than $20 million – and the 
commissioner has not told you that you must report monthly.
Annually – Voluntarily registered for GST. That is, you are registered for 
GST; and your GST turnover is under $75,000 ($150,000 for not-for-profit 
bodies)
