Question
Steve's IT Pty Ltd supplies a tablet to Lil's Cycle Shop in return for a bicycle and $110 (in cash).
The bicycle has a GST inclusive market value of $550.
The tablet has a GST inclusive market value of $660.
Steve’s supply is fully taxable.
How much GST is payable on Steve’s supply?
a) $60
b) $66
c) $55
INTERNAL
UNOFFICIAL
UNOFFICIAL
Answer
The answer is a) $60. 
The GST payable is 10% of the value of the taxable supply.
The value is 10/11 of the price.
The price is the sum of any:
• monetary consideration, and
• the GST inclusive market value of any non-monetary consideration.
The price is $110 + $550 = $660
The value is 10/11 x $660 = $600
The GST payable is 10% x $600 = $60
Alternatively (as the supply is fully taxable) you can calculate the GST as 1/11 of the price.
1/11 x $660 = $60
