Assurance Hub
INTERNAL 7
Our Assurance Hub supports a tailored assurance approach according to treatment and client behaviour. 
Assessment and Assurance
Assistant Commissioner Daniel Smith
Multi-risk Assurance
Assistant Commissioner Eloise Moore
Our Assessment and Assurance (A&A) branch supports frontline 
operations in the Small Business GST and Income Tax space, with a focus 
on:
• Pre-Issue Assessments
• Education and campaign work to encourage compliance. 
A&A cases generally have shorter cycle times.
Our Multi-risk Assurance branch focuses on the small business 
population, addressing multiple risks through reviews and audits. 
These cases generally have medium to longer term cycle times, and
involve a broad range of issues and a spectrum of behaviours, from willing 
compliance to deliberately avoidance.
Complex Arrangements Assurance
Assistant Commissioner Emma Butler
Shadow Economy Program & Third-Party Reporting
Assistant Commissioner Julia Webb
Our Complex Arrangements Assurance branch focuses on the small 
business population, addressing multiple risks through reviews and audits. 
Complex arrangements cases generally have longer cycle times, involving 
more in-depth analysis and investigation, and tend to encounter a higher 
frequency of deliberately avoidant behaviours. 
Our Shadow Economy Program and Third-Party Reporting branch 
influences shadow economy behaviours by investing in targeted 
strategies across the ATO. This includes the use of automation, media, 
campaigns, and community events as needed. 
They seek opportunities to optimise third-party reporting, and seek to 
bring greater visibility and assurance to the small business market. 
