Connecting across Small Business 
INTERNAL 14
Small Business Site 
Support
Small Business Site Support Leadership
complements National Site Leadership and 
supports the SB Culture & Engagement Strategy.
There are 19 sites with an SB presence. SES Site 
Sponsors are assigned to their home sites to 
ensure visibility. Where an SES isn’t onsite, an 
offsite SES is assigned so all staff have access to 
a Site Sponsor. For example, a delivery SES may 
support a site with a strong Risk & Strategy 
presence to offer balanced insights.
Find your SES Site Sponsor here!
Site Matter Events
Here in Small Business, we understand the value 
of staying connected across our business line. 
That’s why we hold Site Matters Events. These 
events are held twice times a year, and are run 
by your Site Support Leaders! 
These events bring Small Business staff 
together at a site level to network, connect with 
leaders, and collaborate on key people and 
culture initiatives. 
Staff Engagement
To strengthen our connection across Small 
Business and foster communication within the 
business line, we’ve introduced All-Staff 
Engagement sessions. These sessions are held 
both virtually and locally, and all staff are 
encouraged to attend on-site where possible. 
During each session, you’ll hear updates from our 
Small Business executive team, have the 
opportunity to ask questions and share feedback, 
and then break into facilitated discussions led by 
local Small Business leaders.
Read about one of our sessions here!
